  "reply_text": "**I’d hold the merge for one high-priority bug.**\n\n**`src/guard.js:12` — View-only shares can edit unlocked documents.**  \nIn `share.mask & WRITE === WRITE && !share.locked`, JavaScript evaluates `WRITE === WRITE` first. That makes the permission check effectively `share.mask & 1`, checking **READ rather than WRITE**.\n\nConfirmed:\n- A viewer (`mask: 1`) is incorrectly allowed to edit.\n- A write-only share (`mask: 4`) is incorrectly denied editing.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, consistent with `canComment`. Add regression tests for a viewer being denied editing and a write-only share being allowed.\n\nAll six existing tests pass, but they miss this because the editor fixture has both READ and WRITE. I found no other concrete issues in the branch diff. No files changed.",
